==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Perfect Heracrist''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Dark Heracrist''' at level 30.

==Strategy/Usage==
Heracrist boasts truly insane stats for its recharge and cost, further supplemented by the Strong ability when up against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] or [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies. At level 30 with all [[Treasure#Fruits effect|Fruit Treasures]], it has 255k effective HP and 275k effective damage (35k DPS) against its target traits.

However, this unit has a couple of weaknesses, including its Single Attack, slow attacks, and low speed. so make sure to have [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|wave]] attackers supporting it and wipe out peons. Floating enemies have numerous counters while Aliens have less, but Heracrist nevertheless can be used in a select number of stages to crush any opposition, such as in [[Forest Beasts (Deadly)|Forest Beasts]], where it slice through [[Manic Flying Cat (Enemy)|Manic Flying Cat]] like butter.

==='''True Form'''===
Dark Heracrist is similarly powerful against Relics as it was against Floating or Alien enemies, but due to Relic Fruits not existing, it can only reach 204k effective HP and 230k damage against Relics. These numbers are obviously still quite impressive, and it will definitely be worth the Elder Fruit. Previous points about needing help from Wave/Surge Attackers like Slime Cat or Brainwashed Gross Cat do still apply, since Dark Heracrist retains its Single Attack in True Form.

